```java
final java.util.List<String> names = new java.util.ArrayList<>();
names.add("Alice"); // ALLOWED — final locks the reference, not the contents
// names = new java.util.ArrayList<>(); // COMPILE ERROR: can't reassign
```

```java
// The object itself must be unmodifiable for real immutability
final java.util.List<String> names = java.util.List.of("Alice", "Bob");
// names.add("Eve"); // UnsupportedOperationException — contents are locked too
```
`final` locks the binding; `List.of(...)` (or a class with no setters and final fields) locks the contents.

```java
public class FinalDemo {
    private final String company = "TechCorp"; // set at declaration
    private final int foundedYear;
    public FinalDemo(int year) { this.foundedYear = year; } // set once in constructor

    void demo() {
        final int maxRetries = 3;
        // maxRetries = 5; // COMPILE ERROR
        final var names = new java.util.ArrayList<String>();
        names.add("Alice"); // OK — mutating the list is allowed
        System.out.println(company + " " + foundedYear + " " + names);
    }
}
```
